{"question_id": 77114286, "question": "<p>I have the following table in my_model.sql:</p>\n<div class=\"s-table-container\">\n<table class=\"s-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">NAMES</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">COUNTRY</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">DATE</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">AGE</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">mario</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">uk</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2021</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">38</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">robert</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">uk</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2022</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">18</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">frank</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">usa</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2011</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">55</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">julia</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">usa</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1999</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">80</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p>I need to pivot the table and have the final result as:</p>\n<div class=\"s-table-container\">\n<table class=\"s-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">COUNTRY</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">mario</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">mario_date</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">robert</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">robert_date</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">frank</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">frank_date</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">julia</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">julia_date</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">uk</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">38</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2021</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">18</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2022</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">usa</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">55</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2011</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">80</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1999</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p>I have been able to pivot names by doing the following:</p>\n<pre><code>{% set pivot_cols = dbt_utils.get_column_values(table = ref('my_table'), column = 'names')%}\n\nwith pivot as (\nselect * from {{ ref('my_table')}}\npivot(  max(AGE) for names in ( \n    {% for pivot_col in pivot_cols %}\n    '{{pivot_col}}'{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}\n    {% endfor %}))\n\nselect * from pivot\n</code></pre>\n<div class=\"s-table-container\">\n<table class=\"s-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">COUNTRY</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">mario</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">robert</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">frank</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">julia</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">uk</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">38</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">18</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">usa</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">null</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">55</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">80</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p>but I need help with pivoting dates as well to create columns related _date columns.</p>\n", "title": "dbt pivot multiple columns", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/77114286/dbt-pivot-multiple-columns", "answer_id": 77118509, "answer": "<p>You can write another pivot query for _date columns just like names' query and then join both pivot queries using country column.</p>\n", "tags": ["sql", "pivot", "dbt"]}